# Where the test bed gets BASICVFP: RISC OS Open's Raspberry Pi ROM zip
# (5.30 stable, "RPi ROM stable" on riscosopen.org's Raspberry Pi downloads
# page): zip file, sha256, URL; then the modules taken out of the ROM image
# (RISCOS.IMG in the zip): title, sha256, and where it goes (modules =
# out/modules/TITLE,ffa, pirom = out/pirom/TITLE-ROOL,ffa):
#   BASICVFP      BBC BASIC for VFP (the port's ROM has none)
#   VFPSupport    ROOL's own 0.18, only for a test: its elementary
#                 functions, compared with ours
#   SharedSound   1.20, which lets several programs make sound at once (many
#                 sound players need it): the port's ROM has SoundDMA but not
#                 this. (An assembler module, so it can be loaded from disc;
#                 its Messages file comes with modules/LinuxAudio. The Pi
#                 ROM's SoundControl is a C module tied to the ROM's C
#                 library: modules/SoundControl builds it from source.)
# Not in git: basicvfp/fetch.sh downloads the zip and writes them.
# (The page lists an MD5 for an earlier upload of the same release; the zip
# it serves now has a ROM built 15 May 2024.)
